-- title:
--   Normal fibre model with cusp chart for X₀(p)
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ and $\ell$ be primes with $\ell \neq p$, let $A$ be a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ such that $\ell$ is a nonunit of $A$ (the predicate `LiesOverPrime`), and assume the residue field $\kappa_A = \mathrm{ResidueField}\,A$ of the local ring $A$ has characteristic $\ell$. Then there exists a term of the structure `FibreModel` of level $p$ over $A$ with target field $\kappa_A$ and reduction map the canonical residue homomorphism $A \to \kappa_A$, that is: two subrings $B_{\mathrm{fin}}$, $B_{\mathrm{inf}}$ of the field $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-generated inside $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}((q))$ by the coefficientwise image of the full modular function field of level $p$, each containing the image of $A$ under `constantsHom`, with $\bar j$ and $\bar j_p$ in $B_{\mathrm{fin}}$ and $\bar j^{-1}$ in $B_{\mathrm{inf}}$, every element of $B_{\mathrm{fin}}$ (resp. $B_{\mathrm{inf}}$) integral over the subring generated by the constants from $A$ together with $\bar j$ (resp. $\bar j^{-1}$), equipped with ring homomorphisms $\pi_{\mathrm{fin}}$, $\pi_{\mathrm{inf}}$ into the field $\kappa_A(\tilde\jmath, \tilde\jmath_p) \subset \kappa_A((q))$ generated by the mod-$\ell$ $q$-expansions `jqModC` and `jqNModC`, which carry constants to their residues, $\bar j \mapsto \tilde\jmath$, $\bar j_p \mapsto \tilde\jmath_p$, $\bar j^{-1} \mapsto \tilde\jmath^{-1}$, and satisfy the remaining compatibility fields of the structure (summarised here); moreover this model satisfies `FibreModel.CuspChart`, i.e. $\bar j_p\,\bar j^{-p} \in B_{\mathrm{inf}}$ with $\pi_{\mathrm{inf}}(\bar j_p\,\bar j^{-p}) = \tilde\jmath_p\,\tilde\jmath^{-p}$, and both $B_{\mathrm{fin}}$ and $B_{\mathrm{inf}}$ are integrally closed.
--
--   This is the prime-level, hypothesis-free form of the existence of a normal integral model of $X_0(p)$ over a place of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ away from $p$, in the Kroneckerian-model style: two integral charts ($j$ finite, $j$ inverted) reducing onto the corresponding charts in characteristic $\ell$, with a chart adapted to the cusp and with normal chart rings. It feeds the construction of good-reduction specialisations at $j = 0$ used downstream ([`ModularCurve.exists_jZeroGoodReductionSpecialization_doorPredicates`](thm.html#ModularCurve.exists_jZeroGoodReductionSpecialization_doorPredicates)).
-- source:
